# Pav Law KPI charts

Align to [`BRANDING-LAYOUT.md`](gilded-goose/clients/pav-law/project-picker/BRANDING-LAYOUT.md) and [`REPORTING-BRAND-GUIDE.md`](gilded-goose/clients/pav-law/project-picker/REPORTING-BRAND-GUIDE.md) first — see [`pav-law-branding.mdc`](pav-law-branding.mdc).

When adding or editing charts in Gilbert Guide (`kpi-report.js`) on **any** tab:

## Locked layout

1. **KPIs / Recommendations · 2 chart cards side by side** — wrap in `chartPairGridHtml(...)` → `.data-chart-table-grid`. Never publish a lone full-width graph when the section can hold a pair. Odd leftovers sit in the left cell of the next row.
2. **Data tab · plot left, descriptive table right** — stack full-width cards in `.data-chart-table-stack`. Inside each card, `chartBlock()` wraps plot + table in `.kpi-chart-split` / `.kpi-chart-desc` so the graph is left and the breakdown table is right. Graph SVGs stay inside the plot column. Do not use the two-card pair grid for Data when that crushes the split.
3. **Each card** uses `chartBlock()`:
   - required title only in `.kpi-chart-head` — no subtitle, no period/source subhead
   - plot
   - **no color key under the plot** — series identity lives in the detail table swatches only
   - **detail / breakdown table always visible** — never hide behind “Show table”
4. KPI goal tiles and Financial Breakdown text tiles are not chart cards — this lock is for `chartBlock` graphs only.

## Series colors

Unique, high-contrast series colors. **No teal/cyan.** Locked palette:

- Cases / Military / primary → `#3a1a6e` (royal / `--gg-series-1`)
- Digital / Search / Core DV → `#c45c26` (burnt orange / `--gg-series-2`)
- Website / HubSpot / NTGUILT / referral → `#b23a78` (rose / `--gg-series-3`)
- Neutral / unavailable → `#64748b` (slate / `--gg-series-4`)
- LSA / intake → `#1e3a8a` (royal blue / `--gg-royal-blue`)
- Spend / cost → `#6a5acd` (plum / `--gg-plum`)
- **Gold is never an ordinary chart category.**

## Formatting

- Labeled axes/ticks, plot background (`--gg-chart-plot`), baseline, totals above columns, month labels under bars.
- **Month ordering:** charts oldest → newest left to right. Detail-table month rows current → oldest.
- **Y-scale headroom:** top of scale ≥ one integer above highest data point. Use `chartAxisMax()` / `axisMaxAboveData()` / `niceAxisMax()`.
- **Value labels:** `--gg-brown` or `#111` by default. Never white on bars.
- **Monthly Revenue cash labels:** ≥ $100k = green `#1f8a65` via `cashBarLabelFill()`. Below $100k and under the month target = red. Do not force red on $100k+ months only because they miss the $150k goal line.
- **No overlap:** use `barLabelY()` for totals above bars and `chartTopAnnoY()` for Avg / target captions in the top pad. Never put a reference-line label on the dashed line where it collides with a bar total. Skip the on-bar total when the same amount is already in the top annotation.
- Positive counts never red. Red only for negative MoM / negative values, except Monthly Revenue under-target cash under $100k.
- **Plot density:** bars fill the field. Single series ~75–80% of slot width; paired practice bars ~85–90%. Data / stacked plots: value labels 15–16px, category 15px, axis 13px. No inline 9px value labels. Prefer taller plots (~340–380) over sparse short charts. See BRANDING-LAYOUT §6 and REPORTING-BRAND-GUIDE §7.

## Detail tables

- Include period columns, deltas, MoM, and spend/share when the data exists.
- Swatch + series name in the first column when multi-color.
- Totals row when summing adds clarity.

## Channel classification

- **#17 Referrals** — people/partner referral paths only. Do not list Google Business Profile as a referral.
- GBP may appear under **#16 Reviews**, not under referrals.
